1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:40,324 --> 00:01:43,704
You Are a Meat Robot The usual objection to curing all disease is that it's

8
00:01:43,704 --> 00:01:44,344
impossible.

9
00:01:44,884 --> 00:01:48,124
You replace three hundred and thirty billion cells a day.

10
00:01:48,744 --> 00:01:50,704
You three-D-print windpipes.

11
00:01:50,784 --> 00:01:53,244
You reprogram skin into brain cells.

12
00:01:53,764 --> 00:01:57,884
You've already proven your body is a machine, and machines are repairable.

13
00:01:58,524 --> 00:02:01,784
The only reason you haven't repaired it is that you spent the repair budget

14
00:02:01,784 --> 00:02:02,644
on missiles.

15
00:02:03,144 --> 00:02:07,164
This chapter removes the "impossible" objection so you can get back to the

16
00:02:07,164 --> 00:02:10,324
"expensive" objection, which the treaty solves.

17
00:02:10,804 --> 00:02:12,514
Your body is a machine.

18
00:02:12,564 --> 00:02:14,044
Not "like" a machine.

19
00:02:14,104 --> 00:02:14,724
A machine.

20
00:02:15,264 --> 00:02:16,044
Blueprint:

21
00:02:16,044 --> 00:02:16,544
D.N.A.

22
00:02:16,944 --> 00:02:17,504
Moving parts:

23
00:02:17,984 --> 00:02:18,484
organs.

24
00:02:18,784 --> 00:02:19,384
Fuel:

25
00:02:19,424 --> 00:02:22,024
whatever you ate for lunch (usually something beige).

26
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:23,784
Owner's manual:

27
00:02:23,864 --> 00:02:27,844
your genome, which you only discovered twenty years ago, in a drawer you

28
00:02:27,844 --> 00:02:30,544
hadn't opened for two hundred thousand years.

29
00:02:31,164 --> 00:02:33,944
Before that you were just shaking it and hoping.

30
00:02:34,244 --> 00:02:35,264
This is called "medicine.".

31
00:02:36,224 --> 00:02:36,844
Your D.N.A.

32
00:02:37,084 --> 00:02:41,704
is a program written three point eight billion years ago by a process with

33
00:02:41,704 --> 00:02:46,584
no quality assurance team, no project manager, and no version control.

34
00:02:47,044 --> 00:02:48,254
It has never been debugged.

35
00:02:48,564 --> 00:02:49,864
It has never been patched.

36
00:02:50,224 --> 00:02:54,904
It contains code from organisms that went extinct five hundred million years

37
00:02:54,904 --> 00:02:55,404
ago.

38
00:02:56,224 --> 00:03:01,124
You are running legacy software that predates multicellular life, and you

39
00:03:01,124 --> 00:03:02,464
are surprised when it crashes.

40
00:03:03,324 --> 00:03:06,884
That's like being surprised when a three point eight billion year old car

41
00:03:06,884 --> 00:03:07,784
breaks down.

42
00:03:08,184 --> 00:03:09,994
The surprising part is that it starts.

43
00:03:11,164 --> 00:03:13,774
Death is a Technical Problem.

44
00:03:14,184 --> 00:03:17,904
Every religion and philosopher has sold you the same story:

45
00:03:18,024 --> 00:03:18,834
death is natural,

46
00:03:19,484 --> 00:03:20,964
inevitable, and meaningful.

47
00:03:21,604 --> 00:03:22,104
Very comforting.

48
00:03:22,784 --> 00:03:23,284
Also wrong.

49
00:03:24,084 --> 00:03:27,784
Death is what happens when your parts break faster than your body can fix

50
00:03:27,784 --> 00:03:28,284
them.

51
00:03:28,684 --> 00:03:29,204
That's not philosophy.

52
00:03:30,064 --> 00:03:31,664
That's a maintenance schedule.

53
00:03:32,084 --> 00:03:34,464
Every disease is a mechanical failure.

54
00:03:34,704 --> 00:03:36,404
Every ailment is a broken part.

55
00:03:36,924 --> 00:03:41,704
Every slow decline into decrepitude is an engineering problem with an engineering

56
00:03:41,704 --> 00:03:42,544
solution.

57
00:03:43,084 --> 00:03:47,184
You just keep filing them under "philosophy" and "the human condition,"

58
00:03:47,744 --> 00:03:50,384
which is like filing a flat tire under "existentialism.".

59
00:03:51,804 --> 00:03:56,064
You've spent two hundred thousand years writing poetry about death.

60
00:03:56,144 --> 00:03:58,124
You could have spent it building a wrench.

61
00:03:58,684 --> 00:04:00,744
You did eventually build the wrench.

62
00:04:00,744 --> 00:04:02,724
Then you wrote poetry about the wrench.

63
00:04:03,464 --> 00:04:06,134
You Are a Self-Repairing Meat Robot.

64
00:04:06,704 --> 00:04:07,564
Your D.N.A.

65
00:04:07,744 --> 00:04:10,164
is three billion letters of code.

66
00:04:10,264 --> 00:04:11,604
Not "like" code.

67
00:04:11,624 --> 00:04:12,684
It IS code.

68
00:04:13,124 --> 00:04:17,164
You learned to read it (the Human Genome Project) and you're learning to

69
00:04:17,164 --> 00:04:18,644
edit it (CRISPR).

70
00:04:19,504 --> 00:04:23,324
You are mechanics who finally found the service manual under the seat.

71
00:04:24,144 --> 00:04:27,934
The service manual is written in a language you only partially understand,

72
00:04:28,524 --> 00:04:31,444
in a font that's three point eight billion years old.

73
00:04:31,924 --> 00:04:32,424
But still.

74
00:04:32,744 --> 00:04:33,244
Progress.

75
00:04:34,104 --> 00:04:37,584
Every day, your body runs a maintenance routine that would make a German

76
00:04:37,584 --> 00:04:42,764
car engineer weep with joy and then immediately resign out of inadequacy:

77
00:04:43,424 --> 00:04:47,424
You replace three hundred and thirty billion cells daily.

78
00:04:47,864 --> 00:04:49,404
That's three hundred and thirty billion.

79
00:04:49,904 --> 00:04:50,604
With a B.

80
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:55,544
Every day you throw away more cells than there are stars in the Milky Way

81
00:04:55,544 --> 00:04:57,624
and grow new ones before lunch.

82
00:04:58,404 --> 00:05:00,784
You repair ten thousand D.N.A.

83
00:05:01,004 --> 00:05:02,504
damage events in every cell,

84
00:05:03,164 --> 00:05:03,664
every day.

85
00:05:04,084 --> 00:05:06,524
You have thirty-seven trillion cells.

86
00:05:06,844 --> 00:05:12,064
That's three hundred and seventy quadrillion repairs per day, performed

87
00:05:12,064 --> 00:05:14,624
by molecules that have never been to medical school.

88
00:05:15,804 --> 00:05:19,244
You rebuild your entire skeleton every ten years.

89
00:05:19,884 --> 00:05:22,634
You are not the same skeleton you were a decade ago.

90
00:05:23,024 --> 00:05:26,504
You are a ship of Theseus made of calcium and poor decisions.

91
00:05:27,364 --> 00:05:29,334
You are not a static object.

92
00:05:29,764 --> 00:05:33,504
You are a pattern that persists while matter flows through you.

93
00:05:34,144 --> 00:05:38,064
Like a river, except the river is meat and it's arguing with its insurance

94
00:05:38,064 --> 00:05:38,704
company.

95
00:05:39,404 --> 00:05:43,484
Aging is what happens when the river starts cutting corners on its own maintenance.

96
00:05:44,504 --> 00:05:50,024
You are literally dissolving at the molecular level, right now, while reading

97
00:05:50,024 --> 00:05:50,744
this sentence.

98
00:05:51,724 --> 00:05:52,224
It's fine.

99
00:05:52,764 --> 00:05:53,824
(It is not fine.).

100
00:05:54,744 --> 00:05:57,084
You've Already Started Fixing the Machine.

101
00:05:58,024 --> 00:05:58,763
Exhibit A:

102
00:05:59,204 --> 00:06:00,284
You Can Grow New Parts.

103
00:06:01,124 --> 00:06:06,044
A kid in Michigan has a three-D-printed windpipe keeping him alive.

104
00:06:06,624 --> 00:06:10,104
You print custom titanium skulls and jaws.

105
00:06:10,484 --> 00:06:15,154
You grow bladders and blood vessels in labs and install them in humans.

106
00:06:15,464 --> 00:06:16,744
Like replacement parts.

107
00:06:17,244 --> 00:06:17,884
For people.

108
00:06:18,424 --> 00:06:19,034
From a printer.

109
00:06:20,064 --> 00:06:24,524
The same technology you use to print novelty phone cases, you're using to

110
00:06:24,524 --> 00:06:25,364
print throats.

111
00:06:26,104 --> 00:06:30,244
You are manufacturing replacement human organs on the same type of machine

112
00:06:30,244 --> 00:06:32,284
that makes Yoda figurines.

113
00:06:33,004 --> 00:06:36,484
If that doesn't prove you're a machine, I'm not sure what level of evidence

114
00:06:36,484 --> 00:06:37,274
you require.

115
00:06:37,824 --> 00:06:41,184
Perhaps someone could print you a new brain so you can process it.

116
00:06:42,304 --> 00:06:43,584
Exhibit B:

117
00:06:43,764 --> 00:06:45,464
You Can Reprogram Your Cells.

118
00:06:46,124 --> 00:06:50,584
In two thousand and six, Shinya Yamanaka figured out how to turn adult cells

119
00:06:50,584 --> 00:06:52,144
back into stem cells.

120
00:06:53,004 --> 00:06:53,584
Any cell.

121
00:06:53,804 --> 00:06:55,374
From anywhere in your body.

122
00:06:55,864 --> 00:06:57,124
Back to factory settings.

123
00:06:57,684 --> 00:07:00,844
Like holding down the reset button, except on a skin cell.

124
00:07:01,464 --> 00:07:01,964
And it works.

125
00:07:03,004 --> 00:07:03,644
This means:

126
00:07:03,964 --> 00:07:06,224
Your skin cell can become a heart cell.

127
00:07:06,784 --> 00:07:09,084
Your blood cell can become a brain cell.

128
00:07:10,044 --> 00:07:12,484
Any cell can become any other cell.

129
00:07:13,364 --> 00:07:17,004
It's like discovering every part of your car can transform into any other

130
00:07:17,004 --> 00:07:17,504
part.

131
00:07:18,044 --> 00:07:18,724
Need a new transmission?

132
00:07:19,344 --> 00:07:20,784
Just reprogram your floor mat.

133
00:07:21,404 --> 00:07:22,084
Need a new engine?

134
00:07:22,304 --> 00:07:25,464
Your cup holder has been an engine this entire time.

135
00:07:25,884 --> 00:07:26,444
It just forgot.

136
00:07:27,644 --> 00:07:32,104
You won a Nobel Prize for proving that your cells have no idea what they

137
00:07:32,104 --> 00:07:34,944
are and can be talked into being something else.

138
00:07:35,464 --> 00:07:39,084
This is the most important discovery in the history of medicine.

139
00:07:39,804 --> 00:07:43,894
You celebrated by going back to mostly not using it.

140
00:07:44,204 --> 00:07:45,744
Exhibit C:

141
00:07:45,824 --> 00:07:48,404
You're Debugging Your Code.

142
00:07:48,604 --> 00:07:52,364
Gene therapy is literally finding typos in your D.N.A.

143
00:07:52,464 --> 00:07:54,004
and correcting them:

144
00:07:54,004 --> 00:07:55,884
Luxturna (twenty seventeen):

145
00:07:56,424 --> 00:08:01,144
Fixes blindness caused by a mutated retinal pigment epithelium sixty-five,

146
00:08:01,604 --> 00:08:02,704
or R.P.E.

147
00:08:03,244 --> 00:08:03,744
sixty-five gene.

148
00:08:04,504 --> 00:08:05,664
One injection.

149
00:08:05,664 --> 00:08:07,364
Sight restored.

150
00:08:07,424 --> 00:08:10,134
The entire disease was a typo.

151
00:08:10,324 --> 00:08:12,384
One letter wrong, and you couldn't see.

152
00:08:12,844 --> 00:08:14,344
They fixed the letter.

153
00:08:15,244 --> 00:08:18,104
Zolgensma (twenty nineteen):

154
00:08:18,624 --> 00:08:20,544
Fixes spinal muscular atrophy.

155
00:08:21,064 --> 00:08:24,524
Babies who would die before age two now walk.

156
00:08:25,144 --> 00:08:28,544
The disease was a spelling error in one gene.

157
00:08:28,864 --> 00:08:30,064
You corrected the spelling.

158
00:08:30,384 --> 00:08:31,324
The baby walks.

159
00:08:31,764 --> 00:08:32,534
That's the whole story.

160
00:08:33,584 --> 00:08:39,244
Chimeric antigen receptor T-cell therapy, or CAR-T therapy (twenty seventeen):

161
00:08:40,024 --> 00:08:42,824
Reprograms your immune system to hunt cancer.

162
00:08:43,424 --> 00:08:46,164
Complete remission in "incurable" cases.

163
00:08:46,904 --> 00:08:49,364
You taught your white blood cells to be assassins.

164
00:08:50,444 --> 00:08:54,284
They were already assassins, technically, but now they're assassins with

165
00:08:54,284 --> 00:08:55,024
a target.

166
00:08:55,964 --> 00:08:57,924
You're not treating symptoms anymore.

167
00:08:58,224 --> 00:09:00,184
You're fixing the actual code.

168
00:09:00,684 --> 00:09:04,284
That's like going from "the car makes a weird noise, turn up the radio"

169
00:09:04,584 --> 00:09:07,584
to "the car makes a weird noise, let me look at the engine."

170
00:09:08,164 --> 00:09:11,764
It only took you two hundred thousand years to try the second approach.

171
00:09:12,404 --> 00:09:14,964
The Car Restoration Analogy.

172
00:09:14,984 --> 00:09:19,664
Think of your body as a nineteen eighty-seven Honda Civic with three point

173
00:09:19,664 --> 00:09:21,404
eight billion miles on it.

174
00:09:22,004 --> 00:09:24,844
You already know how to fix most of the parts:

175
00:09:24,844 --> 00:09:25,404
Joints:

176
00:09:25,404 --> 00:09:26,344
Like worn brake pads.

177
00:09:27,184 --> 00:09:28,844
You pop them out and put new ones in.

178
00:09:29,444 --> 00:09:31,764
You've been doing this since the nineteen sixties.

179
00:09:32,564 --> 00:09:33,084
It's boring now.

180
00:09:33,984 --> 00:09:35,554
Boring is good.

181
00:09:35,884 --> 00:09:37,644
Boring means you solved it.

182
00:09:38,504 --> 00:09:39,044
Arteries:

183
00:09:39,384 --> 00:09:40,764
Like clogged fuel lines.

184
00:09:41,204 --> 00:09:45,044
You shove a tiny metal tube (a "stent") in there and call it fixed.

185
00:09:45,664 --> 00:09:48,644
This works surprisingly well for something that sounds like plumbing.

186
00:09:50,064 --> 00:09:50,564
Hearts:

187
00:09:50,704 --> 00:09:51,604
Like a dead battery.

188
00:09:52,244 --> 00:09:56,104
You take one from another car (a car that no longer needs it, for reasons)

189
00:09:56,564 --> 00:09:57,464
and put it in yours.

190
00:09:57,924 --> 00:09:59,044
This is called a "transplant,"

191
00:09:59,824 --> 00:10:02,424
which is a polite word for organ recycling.

192
00:10:03,464 --> 00:10:05,784
You're making progress on the harder stuff, too.

193
00:10:06,544 --> 00:10:10,984
Cancer is frame damage, and immunotherapy is your new welding torch.

194
00:10:11,504 --> 00:10:15,783
Alzheimer's is a bad transmission, and you're finally starting to understand

195
00:10:15,783 --> 00:10:16,424
the gears.

196
00:10:17,324 --> 00:10:17,824
The point is:

197
00:10:18,584 --> 00:10:23,043
nobody looks at a broken car and says, "Well, that's just the car's journey.

198
00:10:23,464 --> 00:10:24,574
The car lived a good life.

199
00:10:25,164 --> 00:10:28,224
We should accept the car's natural transition into rust."

200
00:10:28,904 --> 00:10:30,474
You call a mechanic.

201
00:10:30,884 --> 00:10:32,024
You are a car.

202
00:10:32,464 --> 00:10:33,364
Call a mechanic.

203
00:10:33,924 --> 00:10:34,864
Fund the mechanic.

204
00:10:35,984 --> 00:10:40,104
The mechanic is medical research and you are paying the mechanic almost

205
00:10:40,104 --> 00:10:42,744
nothing while spending your money on missiles,

206
00:10:43,424 --> 00:10:47,344
which are not a car repair tool even in the loosest interpretation of the

207
00:10:47,344 --> 00:10:48,814
word "repair.".

208
00:10:49,364 --> 00:10:51,664
The Proof That Aging is Reversible.

209
00:10:52,864 --> 00:10:54,504
Nature Already Does It.

210
00:10:55,744 --> 00:10:56,604
Planarian worms:

211
00:10:57,004 --> 00:10:58,444
Cut one in half, get two worms.

212
00:10:58,764 --> 00:11:00,084
Both younger than the original.

213
00:11:00,584 --> 00:11:03,504
It's like cutting your car in half and getting two newer cars.

214
00:11:04,124 --> 00:11:09,344
This is obviously impossible, except it happens every day in labs worldwide.

215
00:11:10,604 --> 00:11:12,144
Naked mole rats:

216
00:11:12,164 --> 00:11:15,244
Live ten times longer than similar-sized mammals.

217
00:11:15,764 --> 00:11:16,604
Don't get cancer.

218
00:11:17,324 --> 00:11:20,964
They look like a thumb that's been left in the bath too long, but they've

219
00:11:20,964 --> 00:11:22,244
solved cancer.

220
00:11:22,804 --> 00:11:23,824
You have not.

221
00:11:25,124 --> 00:11:26,464
Bowhead whales:

222
00:11:26,524 --> 00:11:30,884
Live two hundred plus years with no signs of age-related disease.

223
00:11:31,504 --> 00:11:36,384
A whale born when Napoleon was alive is still swimming around right now,

224
00:11:36,804 --> 00:11:37,664
perfectly healthy,

225
00:11:38,304 --> 00:11:38,964
probably judging you.

226
00:11:39,684 --> 00:11:40,444
Hydra:

227
00:11:41,084 --> 00:11:43,184
Biologically immortal.

228
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:48,724
A tiny freshwater polyp with no brain has cracked the code to eternal life.

229
00:11:49,524 --> 00:11:51,004
You have a brain.

230
00:11:51,044 --> 00:11:53,374
You have not cracked the code.

231
00:11:53,444 --> 00:11:54,204
Draw your own conclusions.

232
00:11:55,664 --> 00:11:57,824
Nature solved aging.

233
00:11:58,024 --> 00:11:58,724
Multiple times.

234
00:11:59,104 --> 00:12:00,104
In multiple species.

235
00:12:00,624 --> 00:12:01,864
Using multiple strategies.

236
00:12:02,624 --> 00:12:05,984
You just need to steal the answer, which should be easy because you've stolen

237
00:12:05,984 --> 00:12:06,944
everything else.

238
00:12:07,584 --> 00:12:08,804
You've had empires.

239
00:12:09,264 --> 00:12:11,374
You stole entire continents.

240
00:12:11,684 --> 00:12:13,724
Surely you can steal a jellyfish's homework.

241
00:12:15,464 --> 00:12:18,544
You've Already Reversed Aging (In Mice...

242
00:12:18,744 --> 00:12:19,384
and Human Cells).

243
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:20,904
You've done it:

244
00:12:21,964 --> 00:12:26,244
Significant lifespan extension in aged mice using Yamanaka factors.

245
00:12:27,244 --> 00:12:30,904
thirty-year epigenetic age reversal in human skin cells.

246
00:12:32,164 --> 00:12:34,504
Vision restored in blind mice;

247
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:39,044
not slowed, reversed You made old mice young again.

248
00:12:39,424 --> 00:12:42,444
You made old human cells young again.

249
00:12:42,564 --> 00:12:46,904
You made blind mice see again (which, if you think about it, means the nursery

250
00:12:46,904 --> 00:12:48,764
rhyme is now a research paper).

251
00:12:49,264 --> 00:12:51,214
The farmer's wife is going to be furious.

252
00:12:51,984 --> 00:12:53,584
The mechanisms are understood.

253
00:12:54,024 --> 00:12:55,144
The techniques exist.

254
00:12:55,704 --> 00:12:58,464
You've demonstrated them in living organisms.

255
00:12:58,824 --> 00:12:59,774
This is not theoretical.

256
00:13:00,364 --> 00:13:01,444
This is not science fiction.

257
00:13:01,584 --> 00:13:02,794
This is science fact that you proved,

258
00:13:04,004 --> 00:13:09,084
published, won prizes for, and then filed under "interesting" before going

259
00:13:09,084 --> 00:13:10,344
back to building submarines.

260
00:13:11,404 --> 00:13:13,404
You're not waiting for a breakthrough.

261
00:13:13,944 --> 00:13:15,294
You're waiting for funding.

262
00:13:15,764 --> 00:13:19,504
Which is like having the cure for death in your pocket and not using it

263
00:13:19,504 --> 00:13:21,664
because you can't find exact change.

264
00:13:34,476 --> 00:13:40,016
